<article class="m2-page" id="p-games-black-ops-2" data-group="Games" data-title="Call of Duty: Black Ops II" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Games</p>
    <h1>Call of Duty: Black Ops II</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Set up Black Ops II with a measured aim curve, gun detection and the right Scripts.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--ready">Ready</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Measured aim curve</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Gun detection</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-black-ops-2--required-settings">
    <h2>Required in-game settings</h2>
    <p>Set these in the game before you tune your aim. The app shows the same list on the <b>Your game settings</b> sheet. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">How to set them</a></p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting (in the game)</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Look sensitivity</td><td data-label="Value">Highest</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Look inversion</td><td data-label="Value">Off</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Target assist (aim assist)</td><td data-label="Value">Your choice — the EXO works either way</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Field of view</td><td data-label="Value">Unchanged (121° across the screen, as measured); turn rates don't depend on it</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Plutonium (PC): Gamepad</td><td data-label="Value">Enabled</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Plutonium (PC): frame rate</td><td data-label="Value">120 (com_maxfps 120), vsync off</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-sheet-bo2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1339" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Your game settings sheet for Black Ops II. 1: Your in-game FOV box. 2: the I've set these button.">
      <figcaption>Figure OPS-2.1 — Your game settings sheet, Black Ops II</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Your in-game FOV</b></td><td>Type the FOV you play at.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>I've set these</b></td><td>Tap once the game matches the list.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>The two Plutonium rows are for the PC version only. Black Ops II isn't a PS5 game.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-black-ops-2--aim">
    <h2>Aim</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The aim curve was measured in Black Ops II itself, so your Speed and cm/360 mean what they say.</li>
      <li><b>Sync to game:</b> the app suggests <b>this game: 60</b>. <a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--sync-to-game">Sync to game</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-black-ops-2--gun-detection">
    <h2>Gun detection</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The EXO reads the held gun's name from the HUD. Needs HDMI through the EXO.</li>
      <li>The built-in gun reader frame was set for Black Ops II, so most players don't need to move it.</li>
      <li>Give each gun its own Scripts in <b>AI Scripts</b>. <a href="#p-auto-per-gun-scripts">Per-gun Scripts</a></li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ai-list.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="AI Scripts for Black Ops II: Gun out now PDW-57, Gun reader frame, Game settings, Quick scripts and the weapon classes.">
      <figcaption>Figure OPS-2.2 — AI Scripts on a Black Ops II config</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-black-ops-2--recommended-scripts">
    <h2>Recommended Scripts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Aim hold</b> (the ready-made Aim without holding it) comes with the game pack, switched off. Switch it on if you prefer tap to aim. <a href="#p-recipes-toggle-aim">Tap to aim</a></li>
      <li><b>Anti-recoil:</b> Black Ops II has random recoil, so the Anti-Recoil Lab offers <b>Standard pull-down</b> only. <a href="#p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil">Simple anti-recoil</a></li>
      <li><b>Rapid fire</b> for semi-auto guns. <a href="#p-recipes-rapid-fire">Rapid fire</a></li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-bo2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Anti-Recoil Lab in Black Ops II: Automatic isn't supported because the recoil is random. 1: Standard pull-down.">
      <figcaption>Figure OPS-2.3 — Anti-Recoil Lab in Black Ops II</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Standard pull-down</b></td><td>A steady pull while you hold Fire.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-black-ops-2--help">
    <h2>If something's off</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-help-gun-detection">Wrong gun or no gun detected</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-games-mw4" data-group="Games" data-title="Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4" data-time="5 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Games</p>
    <h1>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Set up MW4 with a measured aim curve, fast gun detection and recoil help.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--ready">Ready</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Measured aim curve</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Gun detection</span><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-mw4--required-settings">
    <h2>Required in-game settings</h2>
    <p>Set these in the game, then confirm them on the app's <b>Your game settings</b> sheet. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">How to set them</a></p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting (in the game)</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Horizontal Stick Sensitivity</td><td data-label="Value">4.00 recommended. Any value works: type yours into the app.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Vertical Stick Sensitivity</td><td data-label="Value">4.00 recommended. Any value works: type yours into the app.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Right Stick Min</td><td data-label="Value">10</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Right Stick Max</td><td data-label="Value">100</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Aim Response Curve Type</td><td data-label="Value">Standard</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">ADS Sens. Multiplier (Low Zoom)</td><td data-label="Value">1.00</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Aim Assist</td><td data-label="Value">Off</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Field of View</td><td data-label="Value">Your choice. Type it into <b>Your in-game FOV</b> (the curve was measured at 120).</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-sheet.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Your game settings sheet, marked REQUIRED, with the rows to set in the game. 1: your stick sensitivity boxes. 2: Your in-game FOV. 3: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-MW4.1 — Your game settings sheet, MW4 mouse config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Your stick sensitivity</b></td><td>Type the sensitivity you set in the game (4.00 recommended).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Your in-game FOV</b></td><td>Type the field of view you play at.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>Why these must match the game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--warning"><p class="m2-call-label">Warning</p><p>FOV changes how fast MW4 turns. If the app's FOV doesn't match the game's, every turn is off. Change both together.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-mw4--aim">
    <h2>Aim</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The aim curve was measured in MW4 itself. Warzone uses the same measurement.</li>
      <li><b>Sync to game:</b> the app suggests <b>this game: 120</b>. <a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--sync-to-game">Sync to game</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-mw4--gun-detection">
    <h2>Gun detection</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The EXO reads the held gun's name from the HUD. Needs HDMI through the EXO.</li>
      <li><b>Swaps:</b> the EXO watches the weapon slots, so a swap is caught the moment it happens. It learns your swap pair.</li>
      <li><b>Pickups:</b> tell the gun reader frame which button you pick guns up with (and if you hold or tap it). After a pickup, the next clear read is your new gun.</li>
      <li><b>Firing Range:</b> the gun name sits lower and further right there. Save a second frame as <b>Firing range</b>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Set it up: <a href="#p-auto-gun-detection">Automatic gun detection</a></p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ai-confirm.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Gun reader frame, Confirm step. 1: Which screen is this, with Match, Firing range and Another HUD position.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-MW4.2 — Gun reader frame: save the Firing range as its own screen</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Which screen is this?</b></td><td>Pick Firing range for the range's frame.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-mw4--recommended-scripts">
    <h2>Recommended Scripts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Slide cancel</b> and <b>Aim hold</b> (tap to aim) come with the game pack, switched off. Switch them on in the Scripts list if you want them.</li>
      <li><b>Anti-Recoil Lab, Automatic:</b> marked Recommended in MW4. Do it in the Firing Range: face a lit wall with a door, a sign or lane numbers on it, and keep the moving targets out of view. <a href="#p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--automatic">Automatic</a></li>
      <li><b>Pull down</b> works too, with no setup. <a href="#p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil">Simple anti-recoil</a></li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-choose.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Anti-Recoil Lab on an MW4 mouse config: how do you want to make it. 1: Automatic, Recommended. 2: Manual. Below: Pull down.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-MW4.3 — Anti-Recoil Lab on MW4</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Automatic</b></td><td>The EXO watches your bullet marks on a wall.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Manual</b></td><td>You trace each shot mark yourself.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--important"><p class="m2-call-label">Important</p><p>Automatic and Manual recoil are new in MW4. Check the result with <b>Test it with the gun</b> before you rely on it. Follow each game's and event's rules; Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-mw4--help">
    <h2>If something's off</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-help-gun-detection">Wrong gun or no gun detected</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-games-warzone" data-group="Games" data-title="Call of Duty: Warzone" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Games</p>
    <h1>Call of Duty: Warzone</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">What works in Warzone today, and how to set it up.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--progress">In progress</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Measured aim curve</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-warzone--required-settings">
    <h2>Required in-game settings</h2>
    <p>Warzone uses MW4's measured aim curve, so the settings are the same. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">How to set them</a></p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting (in the game)</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Horizontal Stick Sensitivity</td><td data-label="Value">4.00 recommended. Any value works: type yours into the app.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Vertical Stick Sensitivity</td><td data-label="Value">4.00 recommended. Any value works: type yours into the app.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Right Stick Min</td><td data-label="Value">10</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Right Stick Max</td><td data-label="Value">100</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Aim Response Curve Type</td><td data-label="Value">Standard</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">ADS Sens. Multiplier (Low Zoom)</td><td data-label="Value">1.00</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Aim Assist</td><td data-label="Value">Off</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting">Field of View</td><td data-label="Value">Your choice. Type it into <b>Your in-game FOV</b> (measured at 120).</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-warzone--what-works">
    <h2>What works today</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Aim:</b> measured curve (shared with MW4). The app suggests <b>Sync to game</b> 120.</li>
      <li><b>Gun detection</b> <span class="x2-badge x2-badge--progress">In progress</span>: reads the held gun's name. <a href="#p-auto-gun-detection">Set it up</a></li>
      <li><b>Plating:</b> the EXO keeps your gun while you plate up, so your Scripts don't drop out. Nothing to set.</li>
      <li><b>Anti-Recoil Lab, Automatic:</b> available in Warzone. <a href="#p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--automatic">Automatic</a></li>
      <li><b>Auto ping:</b> a Warzone-only ready-made Script. Every time you shoot, it pings what you're aiming at.</li>
      <li><b>Slide cancel</b> and <b>Aim hold</b> (tap to aim) come with the game pack, switched off.</li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-choose.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Anti-Recoil Lab: how do you want to make it. 1: Automatic, Recommended. 2: Manual.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-WARZ.1 — Anti-Recoil Lab: Automatic (Warzone and MW4)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Automatic</b></td><td>Available in Warzone and MW4.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Manual</b></td><td>Trace each shot yourself.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-games-warzone--help">
    <h2>If something's off</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-help-gun-detection">Wrong gun or no gun detected</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-games-nba-2k27" data-group="Games" data-title="NBA 2K27" data-time="2 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
